The following transactions and materials are exempt from the requirements specified in Sections 9-152 and 9-153: (a) Any materials purchased from a regulated public utility;

- (b) Any materials purchased from an original manufacturer of the material or industrially generated scrap; (c) The purchase of recyclable food and beverage containers from any source; except that, for purposes of this exemption, a metal beer keg shall not be considered a recyclable beverage container;

- (d) Any scrap that is involved in a transaction between dealers or governmental entities; (e) This Article shall not apply to a person or entity that does not provide

remuneration for scrap metals collected in drop-off curbside containers or at materials recovery sites.
